    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0476" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg406"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Campbell</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 17, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 27, of 24th April last,
                    has been received, containing an account of your prompt despatch of a messenger
                    to President Juarez of <pb facs="0477" n="407" xml:id="pg407"/> Mexico, and the
                    reasons why he proceeded by the overland mail route to San Luis Potosi.</p>
                <p>The alacrity with which you executed the instructions from this department is
                    deemed highly commendable.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis D. Campbell,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., New Orleans.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
